- **Forks that are the operator's** — a boundary widening, a new carrier, verb, crossing or public surface, a bundled font or asset entering the tree, a choice that turns what the canvas is — are collected in one file, `evidence/founder-forks.md` in this chunk's work dir, each with what crosses, the rule of ours it meets, its options with their measured cost and its dependences on the others, each checked against the playbook's escalate patterns; none is answered by a default, and the phase stops on them and tells the operator. Technical forks go to the operator as dialogs.
  - Candidates read at the take-up, re-read at P3:
    - [inferred] the placement fix is an engine change for every document behind `custom-widget` (every widget's paint size and placement move), which our rules have so far ratified per change (security-plan, `set_custom_widget`'s attribute replay);
    - [inferred] the route by which a widget reaches the bundled fonts (a public surface of blitz-dom or of the `Widget` trait, or none);
    - [inferred] whether canvas text leaving as pixels in a shot is already inside the ratified crossing (architecture `decision/canvas-crosses-as-pixels`, security-plan `decision/canvas-content-crosses-as-shot-pixels`: a canvas's app-painted content crosses only as pixels in a shot on every ratified carrier), or app-authored text a new class;
    - [inferred] whether a font file or other asset enters the tree (the stand already bundles `examples/seven_guis/assets/DejaVuSans.woff2`; blitz-dom carries `assets/moz-bullet-font.otf`).

